\ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid13788878\charrsid13788878 B. Commands where there is no existing observable interface
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid13788878\charrsid13788878 For example:
\par MSG_SET_PROTO_DRVR_MTU
\par MSG_DISABLE_TCP_FRAGMENTATION
\par MSG_SET_PROTO_DRVR_DBG_LEVEL
\par There is no corresponding GET operation in the code }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid8199746 ZEUK}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid13788878\charrsid13788878  supplied.
\par For those, I recommend a }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid13788878\charrsid13788878 test-only state inspection interface}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid13788878\charrsid13788878 , rather than changing the production protocol.
\par For example, compile a small test-only function into the PRODRV test build:
\par #ifdef PRODRV_TEST
\par 
\par const struct ifnet *prodrv_test_get_ifnet(void)
\par \{
\par     return g_ifp;
\par \}
\par 
\par const struct protoman_statics *prodrv_test_get_pms(void)
\par \{
\par     return g_pms;
\par \}
\par 
\par #endif
\par However, because }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid8199746 ZEUK}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid13788878\charrsid13788878 r integration harness and PRODRV are }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid13788878\charrsid13788878 
separate processes}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid13788878\charrsid13788878 , the test harness cannot simply call those functions.
\par So the better solution is a tiny }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid13788878\charrsid13788878 test-only diagnostic AF_UNIX socket}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid13788878\charrsid13788878 :
\par                          real production interface
\par mock PME  ------------------------------> PRODRV
\par              control commands
\par 
\par                          test-only interface
\par test harness <---------------------------- PRODRV
\par              state inspection
\par The diagnostic socket is }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid13788878\charrsid13788878 not an ACK}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid13788878\charrsid13788878  and is not part of the production protocol.
\par For example, the test harness could ask:
\par GET_IF_MTU
\par GET_DBG_LEVEL
\par GET_TCP_FRAGMENTATION
\par GET_LINK_STATE
\par GET_CL_PRIORITIES
