\ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid7426121\charrsid7426121 And this gives us a much cleaner verification strategy
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid7426121\charrsid7426121 We can now divide the tests into three groups.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid7426121\charrsid7426121 1. Commands with existing output
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid7426121\charrsid7426121 For example:
