r IPC mechanism returns the modified buffer to the sender}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid7426121\charrsid7426121 . If it doesn't, we'll use the test diagnostic mechanism.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid7426121\charrsid7426121 2. Commands with state that another production command can query
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid7426121\charrsid7426121 For example:
\par MSG_SET_CL_PRIORITY
\par        \u8595\'3f
\par MSG_GET_CL_PRIORITY
\par        \u8595\'3f
\par verify
\par and:
\par MSG_PUT_CLP_PRIORITIES
\par        \u8595\'3f
\par MSG_GET_CL_PRIORITIES
\par        \u8595\'3f
\par verify
\par These are ideal because they require }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid7426121\charrsid7426121 no test instrumentation}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid7426121\charrsid7426121 .
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid7426121\charrsid7426121 3. Commands with internal side effects and no existing query
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid7426121\charrsid7426121 For example:
\par MSG_SET_PROTO_DRV_DBG_LEVEL
\par MSG_SET_PROTO_DRV_MTU
\par MSG_DISABLE_TCP_FRAGMENTATION
\par MSG_ENABLE_LINK
\par MSG_DISABLE_LINK
\par MSG_FLUSH
\par MSG_DELETE_LINK
\par MSG_INITIALISE_COMPRESSION_DICTIONARY
\par MSG_INITIALISE_TX_COMPRESSION_DICTIONARY
\par MSG_INITIALISE_REPLAY_COUNTERS
\par MSG_INITIALISE_FLOW
\par For these, we need to inspect the state that the command changes.
\par The cleanest approach remains a }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid7426121\charrsid7426121 test-only diagnostic interface}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid7426121\charrsid7426121 
, compiled only into the integration-test build. That lets the test harness ask PRODRV what state it has reached without altering the real PME/PRODRV message protocol.
